cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DL-TerrainMapper"
message: "If you use this tool in a publication or in teaching, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Marc
    family-names: Ihle
    affiliation: "Digital Landscapes"
    email: marc.ihle@digital-landscapes.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/DLandscapes/dl-terrain-mapper"
url: "https://digital-landscapes.com/"
abstract: >-
  A laser-cut map compiler. Terrain and field observations go in; a fabricable
  drawing comes out — engraved contours, labelled heights, located photograph
  marks, hachures, halftones, sections and thresholded material regions — where
  the symbology maps to laser operations instead of to screen pixels. One
  raster can be translated several ways at once: the value as a line's
  position, as a symbol's size, as the density of ink, or as height against
  distance along a cut.
keywords:
  - landscape architecture
  - terrain model
  - laser cutting
  - cartography
  - GeoTIFF
  - digital fabrication
